WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.605 --> 00:00:05.595
You or someone you know may have been diagnosed with

00:00:05.595 --> 00:00:08.835
type 1 diabetes

00:00:08.835 --> 00:00:11.735
this video will help you understand what it is and

00:00:11.735 --> 00:00:14.955
why is it important to keep it under control

00:00:14.955 --> 00:00:17.745
Type 1 diabetes is a condition where your pancreas makes

00:00:17.745 --> 00:00:20.815
little or no insulin

00:00:20.815 --> 00:00:23.655
insulin is a chemical in your body to keep your blood sugar

00:00:23.655 --> 00:00:25.045
at a normal level.

00:00:25.465 --> 00:00:28.425
Carbohydrates are substances your body uses

00:00:28.425 --> 00:00:30.955
to make energy.

00:00:30.955 --> 00:00:33.995
after you eat food that contains carbohydrates

00:00:33.995 --> 00:00:37.045
it eventually goes to your small intestine. in your small intestine

00:00:37.045 --> 00:00:39.155
the food is broken down

00:00:39.155 --> 00:00:42.355
into single sugar molecules called glucose.

00:00:43.515 --> 00:00:46.445
the cells in your small intestine soak up the sugers

00:00:46.445 --> 00:00:49.555
which pass  into your bloodstream

00:00:49.815 --> 00:00:52.795
When the blood reaches your  pancreas

00:00:52.795 --> 00:00:55.175
it detects the higher amount of sugar in your blood

00:00:55.915 --> 00:00:58.955
normally it causes the pancreas to put insulin

00:00:58.955 --> 00:01:01.965
into your bloodstream

00:01:01.965 --> 00:01:04.755
The insulin reduces the amount of sugar in your blood to a healthy level

00:01:04.755 --> 00:01:07.895
how does insulin do this

00:01:08.585 --> 00:01:11.705
as the blood move through your body

00:01:11.705 --> 00:01:14.425
The insulin and  sugar exit the bloodstream into your tissues

00:01:14.425 --> 00:01:16.705
to reach your cells

00:01:18.415 --> 00:01:21.605
most cells have structure on their surfaces

00:01:21.605 --> 00:01:25.055
called insulin receptors when  insulin flows by

00:01:25.055 --> 00:01:27.565
it attaches to the receptor

00:01:27.945 --> 00:01:31.145
The insulin acts like a key in a lock

00:01:31.255 --> 00:01:32.255
to open up the cell

00:01:34.695 --> 00:01:36.735
so the sugars can get inside

00:01:37.625 --> 00:01:40.385
now  your Cells can use the sugar to make the energy

00:01:40.385 --> 00:01:42.885
it needs to work properly

00:01:43.225 --> 00:01:46.255
and  your blood sugar level drops back to its normal range

00:01:49.585 --> 00:01:52.595
if you have  type 1 diabetes

00:01:52.595 --> 00:01:54.995
your pancreas lose its ability to make enough

00:01:54.995 --> 00:01:56.135
or any insulin

00:01:57.285 --> 00:02:00.265
this can result in high blood sugar level

00:02:00.265 --> 00:02:01.945
and other complications

00:02:02.815 --> 00:02:04.925
in type 1 diabetes

00:02:05.375 --> 00:02:08.635
your immune system attacks your cells in pancreas

00:02:08.635 --> 00:02:10.085
by mistake

00:02:15.305 --> 00:02:18.145
as a result, your pancreas makes a little or no insulin

00:02:22.565 --> 00:02:25.705
without insulin sugar can not get into your cells.

00:02:25.705 --> 00:02:28.435
Without  sugars

00:02:28.435 --> 00:02:29.435
your cells  don't have energy.

00:02:31.485 --> 00:02:34.455
and since the sugar is locked out of your cells

00:02:34.455 --> 00:02:37.365
it builds up to a higher level in your bloodstream

00:02:37.415 --> 00:02:40.005
this is a condition called hyperglycemia

00:02:40.005 --> 00:02:43.185
which can leads to serious complication.

00:02:44.945 --> 00:02:47.975
 

00:02:47.975 --> 00:02:51.105
 

00:02:51.105 --> 00:02:53.835
 

00:02:53.835 --> 00:02:57.145
 

